$DIR/test.p:3:16: cannot use "x" (untyped string constant) as int value in default value of a
    A value of one type is used where a different type is needed: in an
    assignment, a variable declaration, an argument or a return. Plutonium, like
    Go, never converts between types by itself, even between int and int64, or
    between numbers and text.
    Convert explicitly with T(x) between number types, or use a function such as
    strconv.Atoi to turn text into a number.
    (see "Assignability" in the Plutonium spec, section 8.4)
    (run "pluto explain E0023" for a longer explanation)
